\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Gracious Spirit, Holy  Ghost,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thought by Thee, we covert most,
\par Of Thy gifts at Pentecost,
\par Holy, heavenly love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Faith that mountains could remove,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Tongues of earth or heaven above,
\par Knowledge, all things, empty prove
\par Without heavenly love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Though I as a martyr bleed,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Give my goods the poor to feed,
\par All is vain if love I need;
\par Therefore give me love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Love is kind, and suffers long;
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Love is meek, and thinks no wrong
\par Love that death itself more strong;
\par Therefore give us love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Prophecy will fade away,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Melting in the light of day;
\par Love will ever with us stay;
\par Therefore give us love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Faith and hope and love we see,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Joining hand in hand agree;
\par But the greatest of the three,
\par \pard        And the best, is love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

